sources, in application order
  .headwater/packages/acme-printed/taxonomy.yml

operations that make what they address: 0

shelves that print their key for want of a display name: 0

rules
  structural conformance
    over one source: the declarations, their members, every scalar type and every closed set
  reference well-formedness
    over one source: every address and every `$`-reference parses, and stands where one may
  referential integrity
    on the result: every name a declaration reads is declared, every relation endpoint is a kind or an anchor kind, and every control discharges a declared obligation. A name that a `remove` orphaned is reported against that `remove`. The `$`-reference half runs at merge time, because a reference that reads nothing stops the merge
  anchor integrity
    on the result: one resolver per anchor kind, and no two anchor kinds share a namespace
  identifier integrity
    on the result: every scheme carries a namespace, every pattern reads as a template, and no two schemes admit one string. The last is decided out of the parsed segments and not out of the pattern text: a `{slug}` is terminal, so a template is a fixed run of literal and digit positions with an optional free tail, and whether two such runs meet is a comparison rather than an estimate
  coverage
    on the result: every shelf reaches a kind, every concrete kind is reached by a shelf, and an abstract kind is reached by none
  kind inheritance
    on the result: `is_a` names a declared abstract kind, the chain terminates and holds no cycle, no child un-requires or forbids what a parent requires, and a narrowed value set names only values the facet declares and only values every kind above it admits
  purpose completeness
    on the result: every concrete kind has a purpose by declaration or inheritance, every declared purpose is served, and no kind writes a blank `write_when`
  determinism
    on the result: no two shelf patterns can match one path at equal specificity. The overlap is decided over the two patterns, so no corpus has to exist for the rule to fire
  role uniqueness
    on the result: at most one facet claims each role of the closed registry
  lifecycle soundness
    on the result: every state is a value of the state vocabulary, every state a regime names is reachable from that regime's initial state, every state of the vocabulary is reachable in at least one regime, and every state with no exit is declared terminal
  relation coherence (in part)
    on the result: a nucleus–satellite relation names its nucleus and a multinuclear one names none, `inherits` names facets that both ends carry, only a relation of the `evidence` family declares `evidence_at`, and `on_target.set_state` names a state that every kind at the `to` end can stand in
    not decided: "a family's default is not contradicted without explicit override" states no rule that a validator can fail. A declared nuclearity is the explicit override, and the taxonomy model gives the count to `taxonomy audit`
  expectation well-formedness
    on the result: every expectation names a declared relation or a declared inverse, endpoints that the relation admits, a reachable target kind, and an origin facet that the declaring kind requires
  core satisfiability
    at merge time: checked on the result, naming the operation that removed the last satisfier
  facet canons (in part)
    on the result: relevance, ascertainability and permanence, which the taxonomy model states are decidable from the schema alone
    not decided: differentiation and orthogonality need a corpus, and the taxonomy model gives both to `taxonomy audit`
  kind rigidity
    on the result: no kind name is a value of the state vocabulary, and none is a bare phase adjective
  edge provenance
    at merge time: the meta-schema requires `created_by` on every relation, and the resolver validates the merged result against the meta-schema as well as each source. So a `remove` that takes the member out is refused before these rules run, and a rule here would be unreachable
  attribute well-formedness
    on the result: every instance attribute names a value space and an owning end, and no attribute is called `to`
  warrant integrity (in part)
    on the result: every transcription projection pins a declared anchor kind, and that anchor kind names one resolver
    not decided: whether a transcription writes over an authored path is a question about a corpus, and it belongs to the same rule as every other projection target
  context safety
    on the result: every facet that carries the freshness role declares a staleness policy, and every `agent_rules` projection, the one agent-facing declaration the language has, declares a `budget` (HW-DR-0115). No declaration marks a kind agent-facing, so no kind owes one
  overlay confluence
    at merge time: pairwise over the leaves each operation writes, before anything merges
  mapping integrity (in part)
    on the result: every kind and every facet value that a mapping names on this side is declared here
    not decided: the far side. A mapping names kinds in another taxonomy, and nothing fetches or resolves one
  projection targets (in part)
    on the result: every projection writes a relative path that stays inside the corpus root, every shelf path stays inside the repository, and every path a language regime lists outside the corpus root stays inside the repository and answers to one regime
    not decided: the collision with an authored path, which needs the census. `generate --check` is where that lands

not decided anywhere: 0

acme/printed is not valid
